WEBVTT

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.890
Saito, go that way!

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.990
Don’t tell me there’s another fury!

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.470
Wait, damn it!

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.630
Ibuki!

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.890
Are you unharmed?

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.040
Y-yeah...

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.810
You want to put a fury’s
head on display in Osaka?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.850
Yeah. It’s that chief’s orders.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:32.810
To top it off,

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.540
he was another ronin claiming to

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.090
be part of the Roshigumi and
coercing money out of people.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.720
Is putting his head on display
meant to be a warning?

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.100
I opposed the idea since

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.820
the masses will feel even more
hostile toward us if we do,

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.230
but he said a bad name
beats none at all.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.610
Very well.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:00.590
I shall leave for Osaka with
the inspectors immediately.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.140
Sorry about this!

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.740
I always dump the nasty work on you.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.390
Not at all. Do not dwell upon it.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.260
I fully understand what my job is.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.650
Pardon me!

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.140
Is anyone in?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.540
Who’s that?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.640
He here to challenge
our school of kendo?

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.380
I still haven’t asked
for your name yet, have I?

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.660
I guess I might as well ask
while you can still talk.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.600
Hajime Saito.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.150
Saito-kun, huh?

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:52.240
I’m Souji Okita. Nice to meet you.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.910
Shinpachi-san!

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.270
Could you be our ref?

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:58.420
Sure, you got it.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.820
Hey, you gonna be okay?

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.680
Souji is our dojo’s star student.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.360
There is no need for concern.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.190
Begin!

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.270
One hit in!

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.180
H-hey, can’t you hear me?

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.580
You’re stronger than I expected.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.000
No one’s been able to
dodge my thrust before.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.270
You are the first person I failed to

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.060
defeat in my first move.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:02.710
What is it, Toshi?

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.510
What the hell are you doing?!

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.140
Shinpachi! Heisuke! Hold Souji back.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.890
Harada, you handle that other guy!

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.590
My, you were quite impressive!

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.770
I fight using a left-handed stance.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.090
Does that not bother you?

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.090
Huh? Oh!

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.000
Whether you use a right-handed stance

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.920
or a left-handed stance,

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.100
it doesn’t change the
fact that you’re strong.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.360
That was the day...

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.270
...I met people who
acknowledged my strength

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.750
for the very first time.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.490
I will protect the place
where we can be together.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:06:00.080
The Shackles of Pandemonium

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.460
Three Days Later

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.170
Hajime-kun!

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.160
It’s just about time for our patrol.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:12.920
Right.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:14.850
That is all for now!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.040
Seriously!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.600
You’re right!

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.410
It’s the Wolves of Mibu!

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.080
I hear they put a ronin’s
head on display.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:30.860
In Osaka?

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.790
They frighten me!

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:47.220
Damn, every time I go on patrol
people keep callin’ us

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.970
“Wolves of Mibu!”

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.260
It’s such a pain!

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:51.610
What’s this?

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.820
Shinpachi-san, you’re
fragile enough to let

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.640
something like that get to you?

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:58.250
Not me.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.660
Heisuke’s actin’ all depressed.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.650
I can’t stand this annoying mess.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.460
It looks like it’s getting
to our younger members as well.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.370
Oh, jeez.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.920
What a bunch of wimps.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:13.680
The locals are so scared of
us that they open up a path.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.060
It’s easier to get around,
so what’s the big deal?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.330
Right, Hajime-kun?

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.040
Excuse me!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:25.240
Is Niimi-san in?

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:30.050
Oh, I’m afraid Niimi-san’s
out right now.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.110
Is that right?

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:35.500
Sannan-san is also away,
which is why I came here.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.690
I had hoped to hear the story
from them in more detail...

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.230
Come to think of it,

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.190
didn’t you see the
ronin who turned into a fury?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.590
Huh? Well, yeah...

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:50.240
How did he look?

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:51.950
What do you mean?

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.720
If anything stood out to you,

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.950
could you tell me about it?

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.730
Anything that stood out...?

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:00.950
Kodo-san,

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:03.300
Colonel Sannan is back.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.310
Is that right?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.210
Pardon me.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.970
Don’t divulge unnecessary
information to outsiders.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:13.790
Huh?

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.570
Put some thought into you position!

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.580
What’s he mean about
my “position”?

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.870
Okay! That’s it for today!

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:32.090
Thank you very much!

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.150
Ibuki!

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.580
I don’t know what you
plan to do in the future,

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.060
but I will instruct you.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:48.620
Why don’t you learn swordplay
with our other members?

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.260
Nah, I’m fine...

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.830
Once you leave the Roshigumi,

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:56.760
will you be able to protect yourself?

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.230
You will not be fortunate
enough to get taken in

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:01.880
by someone like Serizawa-san
a second time.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:03.770
“Fortunate”?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.900
I am going to ask you a question.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.650
Do you want to live?

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.420
I have a hard time calling
that “good luck.”

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:16.660
Now he orders me around like nuts.

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.160
Start coming here as of tomorrow.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:21.660
No, wait!

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.560
C’mon, Saito!

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.570
What’s gotten into him?

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:34.620
But, true enough,

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.240
what am I supposed to do after this?

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.890
I’m going. I’m not going.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.930
I’m going! I’m not going!

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:48.020
Tardiness is strictly prohibited.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.440
But I never said I was going!

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.550
Since you have decided
to begin training,

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:03.320
you must first learn the basics.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.600
Not that I decided to do this...

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.210
Fine!

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:10.990
Huh?

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.570
Bring your right leg forward.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:15.120
Shift your left leg back.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:15.840
Huh?

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:18.230
Have the sword pointed directly over

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:20.020
your opponent’s head like so.

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.580
This is the basic stance.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:23.480
Okay!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.810
When holding your katana’s hilt,

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:27.650
put strength in your grasp

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:29.830
starting with the pinkie
fingers and going up.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:30.610
Okay!

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.630
Not like that.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:34.610
Like this?

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.420
Don’t hold it from the side.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.050
Huh?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:38.570
When you strike at someone,

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.380
you would have to control
it with just your thumbs.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.350
Okay, got it.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:50.240
There’s no need to teach
Ryunosuke swordsmanship.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:52.450
Why not?

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.630
He’s finally decided to learn it.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.340
That’s right!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.130
If Ryunosuke’s trying
to change, why not let him?

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:05.740
Uh-huh...

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:13.680
Dang it, Saito!

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:17.680
There’s no way I can start
out swinging it a thousand times!

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:21.910
We need him to pay for the tailor fees!

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:25.660
Yeah, but the master is currently out...

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.480
Hishiya gave me

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:30.240
strict orders not to return to our store

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.100
until I receive the money.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:34.570
I am terribly sorry.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:37.510
I will be certain to tell the master,
so please

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:39.050
pull back for today.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.450
Is that right?

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:42.450
Very well.

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:45.680
In that case, I will try again tomorrow.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:01.200
Hirama-san,

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:04.960
what did that lady need
with Serizawa-san?

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:07.430
Well, apparently the master

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:10.470
still hasn’t paid for
the uniforms he had

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:13.210
made for the Roshigumi.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.960
Eh?! He sure pulls some crazy stunts!

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:23.220
Cur, where were you wandering about?

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.270
Start rubbing my shoulders already.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:29.350
I-I’m on it!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:32.280
Pretending you’re away is cowardly!

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:37.420
The dog dares to bark at his master?

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:41.110
You’re a hundred years
too young for that!

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.530
That HURT!

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:52.290
Hey, Ryunosuke! Saito
was looking for you.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:55.250
Oh, that time already?

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.770
What’s wrong? Why the long face?

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:01.030
Haven’t you been working hard at
practice every day?

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.260
That’s great!

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:05.550
Thanks to that, my hands are a wreck.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:10.120
But I still have to attend
today’s practice.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:13.310
And I’ll have a pile of work waiting
for me when I get back.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:15.850
I guess you don’t
leave me much choice.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.190
Come with me.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:20.700
Saito!

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:26.090
I promised Ryunosuke I’d take
him on patrol with me today.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:28.820
Sorry, but could you
give him the day off?

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.330
I see. Very well.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:44.150
Did I promise to go with you?

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:46.610
If I didn’t say that,

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:48.200
there’s no way someone as serious

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:50.200
as Saito’d let ya off the hook.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.470
So you said that for me?

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.220
Just for today.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:55.730
Yeah.

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:59.540
Even so, we risk our lives
when we’re on patrol.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:02.120
A lot of people have
hard feelings against

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.650
the Roshigumi these days.

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:05.690
Don’t let your mind wander.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:07.680
G-got it!

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:10.850
What a dangerous lot!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:11.850
Accursed Wolves of Mibu!

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:14.140
Your reputation’s always sucked,

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:16.500
but it looks like they
hate you even more now!

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.040
Harada-san!

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:21.070
What is it, Sasaki?

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:24.780
There was a ronin that
ran off when he saw us.

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.410
Really?

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:32.740
Well, that’s cute if just seeing
us was enough

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.260
to scare him off.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.270
Don’t let your guard down!

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:37.330
Sir!

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:46.730
Seriously!

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.490
Oh, Sasaki. Not gonna say anything?

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:56.730
Go talk to her!

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:59.140
Knock it off! We’re on duty.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.310
Why the smile?

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:16.930
Huh?

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:20.680
Were you thinking about
that maiko from before?

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.570
N-no,

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.850
I wasn’t... not thinking of her.

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:26.900
It’s just, she kinda resembled her.

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.550
Have you seen her since then?

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:30.510
Of course not!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:33.820
What is it?

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.830
What do you want to do?

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:38.850
I-I couldn’t really say...

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.190
Well, give it some good thought!

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.590
That hurt!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:50.590
Hey, Sano! I’ve been waitin’ for ya!

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.380
Let’s go drink some good saké!

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:54.900
It’s on me!

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:56.930
I’ll pass.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:57.850
Why?!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.230
Goin’ by that smile,
you’re hidin’ something.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:03.600
No good, huh?

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:05.920
Later, Ryunosuke!

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:06.880
Yeah.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:08.860
Ryunosuke!

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.970
You’ll go, won’t you?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.610
Don’t you like to eat
good food sometimes?

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:13.850
Huh?

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.390
But I’m cool with eating
our typical dinner!

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:19.220
C’mon! Don’t hold back none!

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:24.170
Serizawa-san, I’m bringing
Ryunosuke along with us!

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:26.250
Now we’ll have a real blast tonight!

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:26.880
What?!

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.040
You brought Ibuki-kun?

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.880
Serizawa-sensei, are you okay with this?

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.140
Do as you like.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:36.980
Then let’s get going.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:37.780
Yup!

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.640
H-hey!

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.080
What was that about this being a blast?

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.630
Please! Come join us at Shimabara!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.970
What?! I’ll sit this one out.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:49.610
Don’t say that. C’mon, man!

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:52.200
Please, Ryunosuke-chan!

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.280
Cut the “chan” bit!

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.280
I’m begging you!

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.530
Keep a close eye on that wretched mutt

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:12.720
until I finish my discussion in here

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:17.050
so he doesn’t do anything
embarrassing, Nagakura-kun.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.090
I know, I know!

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:20.680
Well, take your time.

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:28.080
At least we don’t have to

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.820
deal with Serizawa-san
for the time being.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:34.070
If you didn’t want to hang out with him,
why not turn his invitation down?

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:35.860
Yeah, I could.

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:38.430
Is it because he’s a big shot?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.390
Nope, that’s not it.

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.980
The fact that Serizawa-san and I are from
the same school is part of it,

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:48.990
but that isn’t the whole of it.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:54.090
I guess I just can’t bring
myself to hate the guy.

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.040
What?

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:59.030
Sure, he does some pretty
outlandish stuff.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.280
But if it weren’t for him,

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.060
Aizu never woulda become our sponsor.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:07.440
It’s a hard fact that the Roshigumi never
woulda gotten up and running

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.100
without him because of funding issues.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.670
He may look like he’s filled
with nothing but flaws,

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.240
but Serizawa-san is doing
what needs to be done.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.880
That’s what I think.

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:25.590
So that’s how you view that guy?

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:29.090
Thanks to him saving your life,

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.960
you got to meet all of us!

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:32.850
Ain’t that great?

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:35.510
I wonder...

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:37.540
Come to think of it,

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.890
Saito said something
along those same lines.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.580
Yeah? But Saito’s no different.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.870
He’s inept, but he’s a good guy.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.400
Good luck with your training!

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:51.750
Yeah!

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:14.780
But dang, Saito’s strict!

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:15.920
He sure is.

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:21.980
We’ve finally come
face-to-face, Serizawa-sama.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:24.660
What do you want?

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:27.040
You know why I’m here, don’t you?

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.980
It would be most distressing for Hishiya

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.560
if you don’t pay our tailor fees.

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:36.050
Sounds rough.

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:48.640
But I cannot give what I do not possess.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:50.980
Surely you jest!

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:53.310
I have been given strict instructions

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.460
not to go back empty-handed.

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.690
My answer will be the same no matter
how many times you come back.

00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:03.910
Tell that to Hishiya.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.960
I have formed my own resolve

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.100
if that is how you feel!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:14.500
Resolve, eh?

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:16.480
Very well.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:17.980
Show it to me.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.400
The Wolves of Mibu are in another fight!

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:49.590
What happened, Toshi?!

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:50.520
Sannan-kun?!

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:52.450
Sorry.

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:53.820
We ran into some thugs using

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:56.360
the Roshigumi name to
forcibly “borrow” money.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:59.670
It turned into a swordfight,
but they got away.

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:04.800
Hijikata-san, Sannan-san,
it’s unusual for you

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.280
to let someone get away.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:11.020
They had a large group
of friends hiding nearby.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.850
I am terribly sorry, Chief.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.170
No, it couldn’t be helped.

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.750
So there are some guys using

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:21.510
our name to steal money, huh?

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.380
And here they were calling

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:26.140
themselves Imperial Loyalists
until just recently.

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:29.070
That simply goes to show how far

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:32.430
the Roshigumi’s poor
reputation has spread.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:34.480
Think putting that head on display

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.440
had the opposite affect we wanted?

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:44.190
That man has been out of
hand lately, hasn’t he?

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:46.840
If the Roshigumi’s reputation is bad,

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:49.680
it could injure the Aizu
Domain’s good name.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:53.620
We cannot allow things to
continue on as they have.

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:30.510
I can’t stand your half-assed stance.

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:32.510
To-to hell with that...!

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:36.600
It is ludicrous for a lowly
cur living in peace to

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:38.390
speak of pride and resolve!

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.400
The Light of a Flashing Sword
